    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5b197f1b_e2f6b1e0",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 467,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T13:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is the dawn+metal backend going to stop advertising this feature? Right now this extension has priority in the RenderPassDesc configuration inside Graphite so we\u0027d still use that instead of managing the msaa attachments ourselves.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 467,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 467,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "85234b43_719541d9",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 467,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T13:49:29Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yes, dawn/metal has stopped exposing this feature. It only advertises LoadResolveTexture feature now.\n\nActually the MSAARenderToSingleSampled implementation in Dawn/Metal currently is a bit inefficient wrt memory management, hence we dropped it and expose LoadResolveTexture feature instead. MSAARenderToSingleSampled is still useful if the backend natively supports it such as Dawn/Vulkan.",
      "parentUuid": "5b197f1b_e2f6b1e0",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 467,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 467,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "062371bc_8a7f3215",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCaps.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 467,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T14:04:15Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That makes sense to me, then we don\u0027t have to change any of the higher RenderPassDesc creation logic to do the right thing on dawn+metal. It seems reasonable that if a Dawn backend could support both features, but there were significant performance differences between them (like metal in this case), it would choose to only expose the best one. \n\nIn the event that they are equivalent, it doesn\u0027t seem problematic for DawnCaps to report both being available, and then we just use the one that\u0027s simplest at the Graphite level, which is `MSAARenderToSingleSampled`.",
      "parentUuid": "85234b43_719541d9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 467,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 467,
        "endChar": 92
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "18ae4148_733d86ec",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-07T14:43:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Shouldn\u0027t this be affecting the pipeline keys we make for Dawn? At least if this is used for Vulkan, it should require new pipelines for every draw in the renderpass (compared to the cases we don\u0027t need to do the resolve load).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "80f25bbc_d6e04d3f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-07T14:58:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Currently this feature is not supported in vulkan backend yet. However, in future when we implement in in vulkan, I am planning to create two pipelines internally in Dawn/Vulkan, one is used by \"resolve loading\" render pass and one without. Then the appropriate one would be selected internally by Dawn transparently from users.\n\nOr we could also require different pipeline keys, we can introduce that change in Graphite later when the feature is fully implemented in vulkan.",
      "parentUuid": "18ae4148_733d86ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "83fed573_7812ed4f",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 8341
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T13:42:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I could imagine it going either way. It seems convenient to have Dawn hide that aspect, and just creating 2 pipelines right away should hopefully avoid a lot of duplicate work since the spir-v should be the same if we\u0027re just changing the render pass description.\n\nBut we\u0027ll likely have some higher-level concept of this loading added to graphite\u0027s keys for vulkan and employ a very similar strategy. At that point, Dawn+vulkan could just as well signal that loading requires a new pipeline just like native-vulkan.",
      "parentUuid": "80f25bbc_d6e04d3f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "21170f8f_2fefb821",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T13:47:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Yeah I think personally I would lean towards Skia needing to explicitly compile each pipeline separately. Seems like always compiling two pipelines is going to lead to a lot of unnecessary work. Or alternatively if Dawn still hid it but lazily compiled the pipeline, I think this is also bad as now we\u0027ll get weird surprise pipeline compiles at times we weren\u0027t expecting it.\n\nAs Michael said, Skia will already know when it is in this situation, so I think it makes sense to have Skia be the one to trigger compiles as it is needed.",
      "parentUuid": "83fed573_7812ed4f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2a41b891_51d43849",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 19434
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T15:03:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think another approach without explicit pipeline differences is that we treat all render passes the same as \"load\" render passes, i.e. they will always have two subpasses. The normal render passes will have \"no-op\" 1st subpass.\n\nIt also makes sense that you want explicit option for Graphite to make the pipeline compatible with the \"load resolve\" render passes. I can add that option to Dawn. However I will need to remove the similar option from MSAARenderToSingleSampled first https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/851116. That option no longer makes sense for MSAARenderToSingleSampled feature. It makes more sense for LoadResolveTexture feature now.",
      "parentUuid": "21170f8f_2fefb821",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bcb27e75_834bd538",
        "filename": "src/gpu/graphite/dawn/DawnCommandBuffer.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 206,
      "author": {
        "id": 5036
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T17:13:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The problem with that approach is older qualcomm (and maybe still new) devices. For a long time their implementation of subpasses was to just create a different renderpass for each subpass. So you get hit by the very expensive load and stores on each subpass. Thus in this case if we\u0027re setting up the load subpass all the time, it can have a big perf hit when it is not needed.",
      "parentUuid": "2a41b891_51d43849",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 206,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 206,
        "endChar": 73
      },
      "revId": "401a04209bbdfe6bfc8a3fc9732b52ec7493303b",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    }
